Fixes from the high-effort workflow code review of the android branch (base 7d21fa5b). Four issues, all reachable from HTTP/MCP/CLI:

1. Host cmd injection (emulator.rs): on Windows start() spawns 'cmd /c start "" <emu> -avd <avd>'. Rust escapes argv per MSVCRT rules but cmd.exe re-parses with its own quoting, so & | " in the AVD name break out to the host. Fixed by charset-validating avd [A-Za-z0-9._-] at the start() choke point (every path funnels here) rather than only at start_android. AVD *ids* passed to -avd are underscore-joined (Pixel_6_API_34), so no spaces needed in the set.

2+3. Device shell injection (mod.rs): input_text only did space->%s, open_app interpolated the package raw into 'monkey -p'. input_text now wraps in sh_quote (POSIX single-quote, embedded ' -> '\'' ). Kept the %s replace INSIDE the quotes so existing behavior holds (input expands %s; metachars stay literal). open_app validates [A-Za-z0-9._] instead of quoting because a metachar-laden package is meaningless AND it closes the 'No activities found' spoof. Rejected the alternative of quoting the package.

4. Feature gate (+layout.svelte): detectAndroid gated on r.ok, but android routes are #[cfg(feature=android)]; when absent the request hits the SPA fallback (frontend::serve_frontend) which returns 200 + index.html, NOT 404 as the old comment claimed -> rail showed on every build. Fixed by requiring application/json content-type (the real status handler returns Json; the HTML fallback does not). Chose content-type over parsing a marker field: cheapest reliable discriminator.

Verified: cargo test -p xpressclaw-core --features android (9 pass incl new sh_quote test), cargo check --workspace --features android clean incl frontend build. Did NOT touch the other 6 review findings yet (connector /test always-ok #5, emulator-5554 vs connector-target mismatch #6, swallowed emulator-start/post() errors #7/#8, unclamped gesture coords #9, screenshot upscale #10) — next up per fahreza.
